(feature GainesvilleAndGulfRailway
      (popup "<b>Gainesville and Gulf Railway (&quot;Grits and Gravy&quot;)</b><br/>"
             "Section between Gainesville and Sampson City in operation from 1899 to 1930")
      (style railroad)

      ;Stations along the route are given in an April, 1915 railroad schedule
      ;Sampson City     0.0 mi
      ;Graham           4.5 mi
      ;Cyril            7.0 mi
      ;Bellamy         11.5 mi
      ;Ellithorpe      16.0 mi
      ;A.C.L Crossing  19.0 mi
      ;Gainesville     20.0 mi

      ;The location of the Gainesville station is shown clearly on a railroad
      ;map along modern SW 6th St. in the block south of University Ave.
      ;The location of the Sampson City station would appear to be at the
      ;railroad's junction with the modern SCL line in Sampson City.
      ;The old railroad right of way north of Gainesville shows clearly in the
      ;topographic maps.  The course from the Gainesville station to NW 8th Ave.
      ;is given in the railroad map.  The rest of the section's course may be
      ;inferred from the Alachua County Property Appraiser GIS map.

      ;Measuring along the measured route reveals the location of Bellamy
      ;Station, which is most likely near the crossing with Bellamy Road.

      (marker
          (html "🛋 Bellamy Station")
          29.762148 -82.272925
      )

